  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is dropped on a spring-mass system as shown in the figure. The block travels <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> meters in the air before striking the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> mass. Calculate maximum compression in the spring, if both the blocks move together after the collision. Spring constant of the string <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.25</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math><br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0082_64473790931f.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" />"
  },
